    <string name="pdf_area_label">Approximate area</string>
    <!-- "Approximate area · August 2026". Separator only; both halves are translated. -->
    <string name="pdf_header_meta">%1$s · %2$s</string>
    <!-- Printed only when at least one day in the range was projected from another latitude.
         The home screen already says this, but a PDF is the one form of these times that
         leaves the app: it gets printed, pinned to a wall and handed to other people, with
         no banner above it and no way to ask it a question. A projected time on paper claims
         more certainty than the same number on a screen. See HANDOVER A10. -->
    <!-- "These times", not "Fajr and Isha". The first draft named the two prayers, matching
         how the polar problem is usually described, and the rendered PDF proved it wrong:
         when a day is projected the engine replaces all six slots from the reference
         latitude, sunrise and Maghrib included. Under-describing an approximation is the
         same class of error as not mentioning it. -->
    <string name="pdf_approximate_note">Some of these times are approximate. This far north the sun does not always rise or set, so those days are worked out from latitude %1$d° instead. Ask your mosque what it follows.</string>
    <string name="pdf_footer">Calculated offline on your device. SajdaTime is free, forever.</string>

